i wanted to ask a little bit  about working with austin again because  i assume he had  something to do with getting you  involved in this project he did have  something to do with getting me involved  i i don't know  uh how it would have shaken out maybe if  he wasn't but  um i'm glad that it worked out for me  because uh  austin when we were filming the pilot  actually it's always extraordinary  playlist we were hanging out  and he was telling me about this awesome  superhero movie about princes and  princesses and  he's just such an incredibly talented  writer who does so many different kinds  of genres so i wasn't surprised  but i know that whenever austin's  involved with something it's going to  have a ton of heart as well  so you know i did the typical  opportunistic actor thing where i just  said like is there a part for me and he  of course went  there actually is and we thought i  thought we'd  leave it at that i think he might have  mentioned it and then  disney plus and adam astro and zanda  vine and all the powers that be  kind of went through their process and  then a few months later  honestly after i've kind of forgotten  about it i got the call  and then was like on a plane in three  days to toronto to get ready  i love hearing how it all comes together  and especially when that gives me  an excuse to name drop zoe's  extraordinary playlist which is getting  a lot of love right now  but still not nearly as much as it  deserves i  appreciate you saying that um we do not  feel  like we're shortchanged in any way uh we  just think  that we are in on a very special thing  that we know if we just keep doing  what we've been doing people will take  note and sometimes these shows just take  a minute  um but um look we're getting plenty of  praise i mean  mandy moore won an emmy yesterday like i  mean we're not we're not the little  engine that could  we're just we know that we can even  reach more people and  we're confident that it will oh i'm  doing my part to make sure that that  happens thank you so with this ensemble  here  you are kind of the old pro on a set  with a whole bunch of  young actors who not all of them but  some of them this is their first  big movie so of all of the movies you've  worked on over your career  who is an actor that you worked opposite  that makes you say now you know  i have to do this on set for them when  they're first starting out  uh this is actually a random one um but  the first person that comes to my mind  is hugh laurie  i did one of the later episodes of house  and it's just one of those moments where  i was playing a sick patient  and you know you'd expect him to be  just a little bit like i'd look i've  done this for 300 people  you know what i mean and and so this  isn't it doesn't mean as much to him as  it did to me  but he went above and beyond to not only  make me feel comfortable  but to give me everything he could every  ounce in fiber of his being  when it was on my close-up when we were  doing our actual intense we had kind of  a fight  thing that we had um i remember going in  the makeup and hair trailer with him he  was clipping his nails because he wanted  to make sure he didn't  scratch me in any of the moments just  like one of those people that  was very inspirational because when you  are the number one person on a set  you do have the opportunity and ability  to set the tone  and um for that reason i only did one  episode but i had nothing but great  things to say and you could see the  reflection of the crew and i really  think that like  that was some really incredible  leadership and i i try to  just be an open vessel when i'm on set  as well  and it was very interesting this time  around being the uh old  guy the the elder statesman um  but uh but but it was actually you know  interesting certain little technical  things that i took for granted that  um some of the kids would ask me you  know about and  and i couldn't believe i had all this  information it kind of was  a reflective moment for me to be like i  guess i have been doing this for upwards  of 15 years like that's pretty wild  realistically i feel like it was just  yesterday i saw you in a movie where you  were playing like i don't know a college  student or something  yeah yeah but you know what i'm glad to  graduate college and uh be a ta  so i also have to ask you about a  certain something you posted on your  twitter account because i kind of love  this possibility hercules have you heard  anything about the song you did  you know what that wasn't as planned as  it seems  i actually during the beginning of  quarantine especially  was playing so much piano my childhood  piano that i got shipped out to la  and i was just going through all the  catalogs and i was laying down a lot and  posting a lot  and also not posting a lot so that was  something that i actually  just had on my camera roll that i only  sent to my family uh because my mom  loves when i just sing in the rafters  and um and then so when i saw that i was  like oh i actually conveniently have  this and so people are like skylar aston  auditions for hercules the thing is  if i was auditioning for the role of  hercules i would act it more  i probably wouldn't be playing my own  piano and i probably wouldn't choose the  michael bolton key which is  literally in the sky um i think the  in the key that roger bart sings it in  the movie it's a lot lower more  manageable  and uh a a little bit more of an i want  song  so when the time comes if the time comes  i'm ready to train i'm ready to prepare  and i'm ready to give everything i can  to hercules if possible if not hercules  i might suggest looking at robin hood  too  i feel like you i don't know i still  can't picture what exactly is going to  happen with that one but i still feel  like  your skill set would very well suit that  role talk to  those producers my agents and my mom who  will agree with you

